* Generic models for the parts whose makers' SPICE models could not be downloaded
* (assets.nexperia.com answered 403 to scripts, 2026-10-23). None of the results in README.md
* hangs on their details: each line says what the model does and how it was chosen.

* BAV99 (Nexperia): two small-signal switching diodes in series. About 0.65 V at 1 mA and
* 1 V at 150 mA, 1.5 pF. The clamps only conduct when the input is overdriven; in normal use
* they add about 1.5 pF to the guitar input. The leakage is set low (IS=1e-14): with the
* nanoamp IS of the usual 1N4148 model, ngspice finds no DC solution with TI's op-amp model,
* and the datasheet's leakage (nanoamps at most, through 1 Mohm: millivolts) changes nothing here.
.model BAV99 D(IS=1e-14 N=1 RS=1.5 CJO=1.5p M=0.4 TT=4n BV=100 IBV=100n)

* BC857B: PNP small-signal transistor, hFE about 290 (the BC857B group is 220-475).
* Generic Gummel-Poon values: the clip LED driver is used as a switch.
.model BC857 PNP(IS=1e-14 BF=290 VAF=50 BR=5 RB=10 RC=1 CJE=10p CJC=5p TF=0.5n)

* Red 3 mm LED: about 1.8 V at 2 mA (N=2, IS from that point). Only its current matters here.
.model LED_RED D(IS=1.7e-18 N=2 RS=10)

* MBR0530 Schottky (onsemi): 0.375 V at 0.1 A and about 0.43 V at 0.5 A, fitted to those points.
.model MBR0530 D(IS=1e-7 N=1.05 RS=0.05 CJO=100p M=0.5 BV=30 IBV=100u)

* Ferrite bead given by its impedance at 100 MHz (Z100), as a resistor in parallel with an
* inductor (L = Z100 / (2 pi 100 MHz)), plus its DC resistance. At audio and at the boost's
* 160 kHz a bead is a small inductor, so the 15 V filter is mostly its 10 uF capacitor.
.subckt BEAD 1 2 PARAMS: Z100=600
Rdc 1 3 0.2
Lb 3 2 {Z100/6.283e8}
Rb 3 2 {Z100}
.ends BEAD
